cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the information in this file when you refer
  to it in publications, and/or if you re-use, adapt, or expand on the
  content in your own training material.

title: 'Using an API to Communicate with a Model'
type: dataset
date-issued: '2026-09-01'
url: 'https://jgarciamesa.github.io/llm-api-lesson/'
version: 'pre-alpha'
license: CC-BY-4.0

abstract: >-
  A 75-minute Carpentries-style lesson for the AI for All workshop (ASU
  Research Computing). It takes researchers who are new to large language
  models from zero to a small working research tool that calls a model
  through an OpenAI-compatible API (ASU RC's openai.rc.asu.edu gateway) and
  returns structured JSON.

